          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A Square and A Cube"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.086,
            0.798,
            0.133
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Which of the following is the greatest? Explain your reasoning. (i) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 7 ^ { 3 }   -   6 6 ^ { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (ii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 3 ^ { 3 }   -   4 2 ^ { 3 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iii) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "6 7 ^ { 2 }   -   6 6 ^ { 2 }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (iv) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "4 3 ^ { 2 }   -   4 2 ^ { 2 }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.407,
            0.162,
            0.59,
            0.187
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "SUMMARY"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.206,
            0.823,
            0.264
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A number obtained by multiplying a number by itself is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "square number",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". Squares of natural numbers are called "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "perfect squares",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.272,
            0.823,
            0.311
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "All perfect squares end with 0, 1, 4, 5, 6 or 9. Squares can only have an even number of zeros at the end."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.321,
            0.824,
            0.38
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Square root",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " is the inverse operation of square. Every perfect square has two integral square roots. The positive square root of a number is denoted by the symbol √ . For example, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\sqrt { 9 } } \\equiv 3 ,"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.389,
            0.823,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "number",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " obtained by multiplying a number by itself three times is called a "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "cube",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". For example 1, 8, 27, ... ,etc., are cubes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.437,
            0.823,
            0.477
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A number is a perfect square if its prime factors can be split into two identical groups."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.485,
            0.822,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A number is a perfect cube if its prime factors can be split into three identical groups"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.534,
            0.761,
            0.556
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " The symbol "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " denotes cube root. For example, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\sqrt[3]{27}   =   3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
